      "id": "b7d898c156fb",
      "title": "OpenAI's upcoming chat-and-work merger in ChatGPT signals the end of all-you-can-prompt pricing",
      "url": "https://the-decoder.com/openais-upcoming-chat-and-work-merger-in-chatgpt-signals-the-end-of-all-you-can-prompt-pricing/",
      "sig": "YJDDy7xIleBzwynX6mZzNq",
      "source": "The Decoder",
      "section": "ai",
      "image": "https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/openai_chatgpt_colors.png",
      "date": "2026-11-01T09:51:06.000Z",
      "summary": "OpenAI combines the Chat and Work modes into a single interface. Starting in December, Plus, Pro, and Business plans will share a common, token-based quota for ChatGPT and Codex. More complex models consume more of this quota, while simple instant chats do not count toward it. In practice, this is likely to result in a decline in ChatGPT’s quality for heavy users on lower-cost plans. The article OpenAI's upcoming cha",
      "why": "A unified quota changes how heavy users consume models and could shift subscription value and usage patterns.",
      "headline": "OpenAI merges chat and work modes; adds token quota",
      "aiSummary": "OpenAI is combining Chat and Work modes into a single ChatGPT interface and, starting in December, will give Plus, Pro and Business plans a shared, token-based quota for ChatGPT and Codex. More complex models will consume more of the quota while simple instant chats will not count toward it, a change likely to reduce quality for heavy users on lower-cost plans."
    },
